<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abdul Jalil IV of Johor</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1721</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Tun Abdul Jalil</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abdul Jalil IV was sultan of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/johor">Johor</a> from 1699 to 1718 and the first ruler of its Bendahara dynasty. As bendahara, the chief minister, he took the throne after the murder of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> Mahmud Shah II ended the old <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malacca">Malacca</a> royal line. Many <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malays">Malays</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orang-laut">Orang Laut</a> questioned his legitimacy, and in 1718 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/raja-kecil">Raja Kecil</a> of Siak drove him from power. He was killed in 1721, and his son Sulaiman was later restored with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bugis">Bugis</a> help.</p></div>
